# .dockerignore for LoopWorker
#
# Rule of thumb: everything the *server binary* needs to compile must be IN.
# Two bugs this file used to cause:
#   1. `web/` was excluded wholesale — harmless for the build, but it silently
#      meant the embedded UI could never be rebuilt in-image. Now stated
#      explicitly: web/canvas (Node/Vite sources + node_modules) is excluded on
#      purpose because the Go server never compiles it; the pre-built assets it
#      DOES embed live in pkg/api/dist and are always copied in.
#   2. No `.git` / `dist` exclusions => goreleaser output and VCS metadata were
#      copied into the build context on every CI run.

# --- VCS / CI / local scratch ------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitattributes
.github
.gitignore
tmp-audit/
bin/
dist/
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.exe
*.tmpfmt

# --- Docs are not inputs to the server binary -------------------------------
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# --- UI: exclude the Node workspace, keep the embedded assets ----------------
# web/canvas = Vite/React sources + lockfile; NOT built inside this image and
# NOT part of the supported product surface (.release/SCOPE-PROPOSAL.md).
web/
# pkg/api/dist is what `//go:embed all:dist` in pkg/api/api.go reads. Negate it
# so the `web/`-style exclusions can never hide an embed input.
!pkg/api/dist
!pkg/api/dist/**

# --- Release/packaging tooling that must not pollute the build cache --------
.release/tools/**/coverage.out
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
Makefile

# --- Editor / OS junk --------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
